==> [2/2] The replication demo needs a second PostgreSQL cluster.
    Follow the step-by-step guide in:
        portfolio-5-distributed-cloud/replication_setup.md

    Quick summary of what you will do:
      1. CREATE ROLE replicator WITH REPLICATION LOGIN PASSWORD '...';
      2. Append wal_level=replica / max_wal_senders=10 to the primary's
         /etc/postgresql/16/main/postgresql.conf  (use sudo runuser -u postgres -- ...)
      3. Prepend a host replication ... line to the TOP of pg_hba.conf
      4. pg_basebackup -h 127.0.0.1 -U replicator -D /var/lib/postgresql/16/replica -R
      5. Edit the replica's own postgresql.conf (port=55432, hot_standby=on)
      6. pg_ctl -D /var/lib/postgresql/16/replica start
      7. Open two psql sessions (primary on 5432, replica on 55432)
         and run the blocks in replication_demo.sql

